a:T73b,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How quickly does the editorial team respond to inquiries?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Our editorial and verification desk strives to respond to all scholarly questions, timetable discrepancies, and mosque submissions within 24 to 48 business hours. Urgent corrections regarding ongoing Ramadan or Eid schedules are prioritized immediately."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can a local mosque submit their monthly Jamat timetable?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Mosque trustees and imams can submit their official monthly schedule using our submission form below or by emailing contact@namaz-e-shariq.com with the mosque name, full address, GPS coordinates, and a high-resolution photo or PDF of the verified Jamat schedule."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What should I do if the prayer times differ slightly from my local mosque?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Our calculation engine computes the exact astronomical entry (Awwal Waqt) based on solar coordinates and classical twilight depression angles (such as 18° for Fajr and Isha). Local masajid establish congregational (Jamat) times roughly 15 to 30 minutes after Awwal Waqt to allow worshipers to perform Wudu and assemble. Always follow your local mosque’s Jamat when praying in congregation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Namaz-e-Shariq affiliated with any specific sectarian organization?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Namaz-e-Shariq is an independent educational and research platform dedicated strictly to verified astronomical calculations and authentic classical Islamic jurisprudence (primarily Hanafi and Shafi’i schools). We serve the global Muslim community with academic impartiality and reverence for the Sunnah."}}]}7:["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-950 min-h-screen py-12 transition-colors duration-200","childr