f:["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-6 sm:p-10 shadow-xs space-y-8","children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 tracking-tight","children":"Detailed Submission & Discrepancy Verification Protocols"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed","children":"At Namaz-e-Shariq, maintaining unimpeachable accuracy in prayer times and Islamic jurisprudential guides is our highest religious trust (*Amanah*). Because hundreds of thousands of worshipers structure their daily obligations, fasts, and communal congregations around these schedules, we adhere to a formal, multi-tier protocol for reviewing submissions and investigating potential discrepancies."}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100","children":"1. Mosque Jamat Timetable Submission Guidelines"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed","children":"We warmly invite mosque committees, imams, and trust boards across India, Pakistan, Bangladesh, the United Arab Emirates, and global diaspora hubs to submit their localized monthly congregation schedules. When submitting your mosque data, please adhere to the following standards:"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Official Authorization:"}]," Submissions must be authorized by an elected committee member, trustee, or official Imam of the institution."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Geographical Coordinates:"}]," Provide the exact street address, district, state/province, and GPS latitude and longitude (accurate to four decimal places) to ensure proper astronomical calculation alignment."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Waqt vs. Jamat Distinction:"}]," Clearly delineate between *Awwal Waqt* (the moment the celestial prayer interval begins) and *Jamat Time* (the actual minute the congregational prayer commences)."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Seasonal Adjustments:"}]," If your mosque implements monthly or seasonal schedule changes (such as shifting Dhuhr or Isha Jamat by 15 minutes during winter months), notify us at least seven days prior to the beginning of the Gregorian or Hijri calendar month."]}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100","children":"2. Mathematical Calculation Discrepancy Reporting"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed","children":"If you observe a divergence between the times displayed on our live astronomical calculator and your local printed timetable, please consider the following celestial factors before filing a discrepancy report:"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"p-4 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700/60","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 block text-sm mb-1","children":"Twilight Angle Method"}],"$L1c"]}],"$L1d","$L1e","$L1f"]}]]}],"$L20","$L21","$L22"]}]
10:["$","$L23",null,{"items":[{"question":"How quickly does the editorial team respond to inquiries?","answer":"Our editorial and verification desk strives to respond to all scholarly questions, timetable discrepancies, and mosque submissions within 24 to 48 business hours. Urgent corrections regarding ongoing Ramadan or Eid schedules are prioritized immediately."},{"question":"How can a local mosque submit their monthly Jamat timetable?","answer":"Mosque trustees and imams can submit their official monthly schedule using our submission form below or by emailing contact@namaz-e-shariq.com with the mosque name, full address, GPS coordinates, and a high-resolution photo or PDF of the verified Jamat schedule."},{"question":"What should I do if the prayer times differ slightly from my local mosque?","answer":"Our calculation engine computes the exact astronomical entry (Awwal Waqt) based on solar coordinates and classical twilight depression angles (such as 18° for Fajr and Isha). Local masajid establish congregational (Jamat) times roughly 15 to 30 minutes after Awwal Waqt to allow worshipers to perform Wudu and assemble. Always follow your local mosque’s Jamat when praying in congregation."},{"question":"Is Namaz-e-Shariq affiliated with any specific sectarian organization?","answer":"No. Namaz-e-Shariq is an independent educational and research platform dedicated strictly to verified astronomical calculations and authentic classical Islamic jurisprudence (primarily Hanafi and Shafi’i schools). We serve the global Muslim community with academic impartiality and reverence for the Sunnah."}],"title":"Frequently Asked Questions About Contacting Us"}]
